Z||000008||mwbackus||07-13-99||03:36 AM||||Ya know, I try to provide whatever help I can to those who have problems or questions if I have any information that I feel is useful.  To date, I have seen absolutly no indication that my input has been appreciated, and it has even resulted in some degree of critisizm at times.  I feel that I can find much better ways to use my time, and I doubt that I will particpate in this forum in the future.<p>       Mike
Z||000009||GREENDANO||07-13-99||04:50 PM||||Mike,<br> I agree.  If you're name's not OGRE, no one listens.<br>  I have a ball joint press that I own and would never dream of beating on a control arm to remove a pressed in ball joint.  That's how you bend stuff!!  Not to mention safety.  I assume we're talking about a rear ball-joint that won't explode appart in your face when the ball joint is free from the knuckle????  <br>  By the way, OGRE, I'm not bashing you!!  You do know your sh*t!  But hey guys, so do a lot of other people here on the forum.  Remember it's easy to guess on diagnosing the symptoms, rather than diagnosing the problem.   You have to assess each problem individually.<br>  I've been working on GM cars professionally for around 14 years, so I also know a thing or two.  :)<br>  Dan-O 
Z||000010||RFMike||07-15-99||10:08 PM||||Mike,<br>I read everything that is written in the posts that may apply to my Fiero.  I appreciate nearly everyone's input, with the exception of those that are obviously bogus. I rarely reply or post, but still enjoy the time I spend.  Your advice was sound; however, some people will only do things the way they want to.  Doesn't make your comments any less valuable.
Z||000011||Pretender||07-16-99||12:20 AM||||the ball joint press?...how much was the deposit and how hard is this tool to operate?...does it require an air compressor?...does it also push the new one in?????...
Z||000012||lowCG||07-16-99||03:58 AM||||You'd have to be pretty good,or hitting that part with a hammer will make the thing go in cocked to one side,not totally straight,and then make the hole in the control arm sloppy.<br>Balljoint presses are pretty much similar to a harmonic balancer puller,except it draws a small round piece through a large yoke.
Z||000013||mwbackus||07-16-99||05:16 PM||||$100 deposit at Autozone.<br>Presses in and out a ball joint with the control arm on the car.<br>Very easy to use and requires no air compressor.  It resembles a very large heavy duty C-clamp, and a large adjustable wrench will work to turn the clamp screw if you are tool challenged like me. :-)<br>You do need a siginificant amount of clearance (~8 to 12") under the control arm to use the press, so a good floor jack is indispensable for this work. <p>Mike
Z||000014||Pretender||07-16-99||08:36 PM||||i want to say thanks!...you guys saved me $70 in labour charges...i got the press from autozone and it worked fine...thanks again!....:o)
